{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QGaussianObstructionAtQ0","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QGaussianObstructionAtQ0","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.qGaussianObstructionAtQ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.qGaussianObstructionAtQ0","kind":"theorem","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-gaussian-obstruction-at-q0.lean#L21-L43","doc":"**q-Gaussian obstruction.** Given the maximal-crossing lower bound\n`q^(m(m-1)/2) ≤ T m` on the Touchard moments (proved combinatorially in the\n`.md`), for `q > 1` the moment sequence is unbounded — the super-exponential\ndivergence. The Bożejko–Speicher obstruction (a positive Fock representation\nexists iff `|q| ≤ 1`) is cited, not proved here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-gaussian-obstruction-at-q0","label":"prop:q-gaussian-obstruction-at-q0","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-gaussian-obstruction-at-q0.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}